    "id": "axios",
    "title": "Replay: axios npm compromise, 31 March 2026",
    "summary": "axios 1.14.1 was published by hand from a compromised maintainer account, with no provenance, and it added the dependency plain-crypto-js 4.2.1, whose postinstall ran the payload. npm removed 1.14.1 at about 03:29 UTC, so a fresh install resolves 1.14.0 again. Sexton marks 1.14.1 Possessed because provenance regressed.",
